        "app_name": "XR Head Tracker Pro",
        "release_date": "1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "description": "XR Head Tracker Pro is a professional research tool developed by Mohammad Elahi at the Vodafone Chair for Mobile Communications Systems at TU Dresden. This Android NDK C++  application leverages the Meta OpenXR SDK to capture and log head-tracking data from Meta Quest headsets, featuring real-time Passthrough visualization. This app collects head tracking information while allowing users to maintain awareness of their physical surroundings through the Quest's Passthrough technology. The application stores motion data as a CSV file directly on the device, providing researchers and developers with easy access to movement analysis while maintaining visual context of the real-world environment\n\nKey Features:\nReal-time head tracking \nPassthrough visualization \nCSV data export\nVoice Annotation\n\nFor technical support or inquiries:\nmohammad.elahi@mailbox.tu-dresden.de\n\n![{\"height\":1440,\"type\":\"image\",\"width\":2560}](https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/75392881_447729551765577_9035669109539332882_n.png?_nc_cat=109&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=iOq-E4k_CuoQ7kNvgH5BrCd&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AYBlMtse_eHE4R0xbEMkiHxvyZmCAy-RGnZPWXyhBPPXMw&oe=67597C00)",
